menu "OTA Updater"

    config OTA_REQUIRE_APP_HASH
        bool "Require SHA-256 for app-partition updates"
        default y
        help
            When enabled, a POST /update targeting an app partition must carry an
            expected SHA-256 (query ?sha256=<64-hex> or header X-Expected-SHA256).
            If the hash is missing or malformed the request is rejected with
            400 Bad Request and nothing is written. The booted firmware is thus
            always content-verified.

            Disable only for development to allow flashing an app image without a
            hash. Data-partition updates verify the hash only when one is supplied
            regardless of this option.

endmenu
